<title>FRANCE: ADP import traffic up ten percent in November 1996.</title>
<headline>ADP import traffic up ten percent in November 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>November 1996 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 46,979 tonnes, an increase of ten percent on the same month in 1995, Aeroports de Paris, (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Global ADP import traffic in November 1996, by region, with percentage change on the same period 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p> Domestic		 2,910 tonnes  up   16.7pct</p>
<p> European Union	 6,557 tonnes  up   41.2</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	  1,253 tonnes  up   33.5</p>
<p> North Africa	     652 tonnes  down 29.7</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa   4,426 tonnes  up    9.2</p>
<p> North America	 14,817 tonnes  up    1.1</p>
<p> French territories     677 tonnes  down 32.9</p>
<p> Latin America	  1,924 tonnes  up    3.9</p>
<p> Middle East	    2,433 tonnes  up   14.9</p>
<p> Far East		11,330 tonnes  up   13.1</p>
<p> Total		   46,979 tonnes  up   10.0</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
